WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.126
- It was just, "Coach, listen.

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:04.921
I understand, I appreciate it. You know what I mean, all the hard work and 
dedication you're doing, but I wanna be honest with you. 

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.256
I'm not coming. I'm gonna go to Miami.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:08.216
- When you committed to Miami, you told him that.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:08.675
- Yeah.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.759
- What was his response?

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:10.760
- He was just like,

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.679
"If you don't come here, man,

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.473
I promise you, man, you'll never see a day of football in your life."

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:16.016
- Wow.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.474
- Yeah.

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:24.107
♪♪♪ 

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:26.067
- Oh, we got another 'Cane great. Devin Hester, 

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.027
what's good with you, man?
- What's up, baby? 

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.278
What's up, baby?
- How you livin', man?

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.779
- I'm doin' pretty good. How about yourself?

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.323
- I'm good, man. You had to rep all
Florida with that chain on, didn't you?

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:33.408
- You already know.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:34.075
- [Laughing]

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:35.285
- Always keep a Cuban link on you, man.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.286
- Got too, man.

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.078
- How's life treating you right now?

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:38.496
- Great, man. I can't complain, man.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.206
- Are you nice on the sticks? I'mma go ahead and let you break real quick.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.042
- I'm all right, man. You know, I do a little something.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:46.671
- See, one thing I learned about y'all 'Canes, y'all be downplaying 
yourselves and then y'all jump on the stick.

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:48.214
And y'all be trying to give me some work.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.717
- You know, we all humble, man. We consume a little bit, but we stay humble.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.968
- [Laughing]

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.136
- Let’s see what you got.

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:56.556
- So we've had a lot of Hurricane greats on this show already. 

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.184
You among the latest to join Untold Stories.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:00:59.809
- Gotcha.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:02.854
- Tell me about your recruitment process going to Miami.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:07.442
- So, man, this is a story that probably 99 percent of the people 
in this world don't know about.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:11.488
High school, you know, you have to qualify. GPA, the SAT, and all that.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.906
My junior year,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.366
took the SAT. Got my scores back.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.912
Had a nice GPA around a 2.9 through, like, a 3.2.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.371
Pretty much I ain't have to worry about school.

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:22.957
At the time, I had a college coach 

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:26.461
that was really, really stressing me out. You know what I mean, trying to recruit me.

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:27.962
- What does stressing you out mean.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:29.339
- He was just calling me every day. 

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:31.841
Seeing how I was doing, what was my decision, what was my decision?

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:34.594
And it got to the point where it looked like his job was on the line 

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.470
if he didn't get me.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.555
I wanted to be honest with him, like, Coach, listen, man. 

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:39.724
I respect you. I'm committing to Miami."

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:40.934
He was like, "Listen. 

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.935
You don't come here,

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.354
I promise you, you ain't gonna to play a down of football."

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:45.105
So I'm like, "Huh?"

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:45.855
- Wait, what?

00:01:45.855 --> 00:01:48.024
- So I put one on. I said, "Man, you trippin'." I hung up on him.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:49.275
He started blowing my phone up.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.779
My mom ended up answering the phone one time. 
And she kinda went off on him, like, "Listen. 

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.781
Respect my son's decision. We're not coming."

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.990
We get checked in the dorms. 

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.325
As I'm walking out the door,

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.284
one of the deans,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.995
he was like, "We need you to come down to the facility. 
There's an incident that popped up."

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.373
They got a call in from another college.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:04.707
- Mmm.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.501
- And some other phone calls 

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:08.837
saying that, "They overlooked your SAT scores. 

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:12.966
They said that your answers matched another person's 
answers that was sitting beside you.” 

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.592
What really made me so upset,

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:16.302
I said, "Well, what did that person score?"

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.679
He said "880."

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:18.596
I said, "What did I score?" 

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:20.014
A 950.

00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:22.809
So who's cheating on whose paper then?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:23.977
They couldn't prove it. 

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.228
All they said was 

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:28.606
another college and some other unknown phone number calling, questioning.

00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:29.774
And he said “Devin, 

00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.568
it don't look like you're gonna be playing this year." 

00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:32.527
So I'm like, "What?"

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:33.444
- Wow.

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:35.405
- So he was like, "There's nothing we can do. 

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:38.283
We're going to continue to fight this, but as of right now, you ain't eligible." 

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.368
- I get back home. My mom know the situation. 

00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:41.828
So I pull up in the driveway,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.371
And they just boohoo crying. 

00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:45.748
You know what I mean? And it hurts me to this day. I hate talking about it. 

00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:48.042
When I walk in my house, man, it's like my life's over.

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.252
I go in my room. 

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:50.712
I shut the door.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.589
I probably was in the room for, like, two months straight.

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.757
- When you're back home, you say you didn't leave the crib.

00:02:54.757 --> 00:02:55.341
- Yeah.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.926
- And the level of embarrassment that you felt.

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:58.678
Did you feel a level of depression as well?

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.514
- It was just like I let everybody down.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.099
Everybody that was rooting for me: 

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:05.685
my teammates, my coaches, my mom, my family. 

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:09.689
Everything they sacrificed for me to get to that stage and to get it taken away.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.900
Just like a person that goes to prison that's innocent.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.277
And then to sit out a whole year.

00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:16.988
Miami didn't wanna take that risk allowing me to play 

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:20.700
and then it come back up four, five weeks later 

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.453
and them play four, five games and now that whole season erased.

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.038
- Did you watch Miami games at all?

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.289
- I ain't watch no football.

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:28.333
I was at the low point of my life where

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.835
I started going back to my high school, helping them out. 

00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:32.045
That's how bad it was.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.380
The coach at that time was like, "Listen, man, I know 

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.843
your situation. But listen. We do need a person like you to 
come in and give us some good work."

00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:40.220
I was like, "Cool, man. 

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.888
Let me know what what time y'all need me there."

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.057
I went back and I practiced with those guys,

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.226
and I was on the scout team. And I made those guys better.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.727
- How did that season play out for Miami?

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.437
- They ended up going to the national championship.

00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:50.813
- So if you would've played, 

00:03:50.813 --> 00:03:54.442
and then the NCAA would have declared you ineligible, 

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:55.235
what would have happened to that season?

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.071
- I think it would erase their games. So now they would've been bowl-ineligible.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.530
- Let me get this shot in real quick.

00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:02.825
- What really kept me motivated, bro, was 

00:04:02.825 --> 00:04:04.744
Miami stayed by me the whole time.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.579
Coach Coker, I tip my hat out to him. I'm like, "Listen, 

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.664
I had No 4. 

00:04:07.664 --> 00:04:08.957
Jersey No 4." I was like, "Listen, 

00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:13.211
show me here honestly that you're going to stick with me 
no matter what and keep my jersey number.”

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:16.381
Coach Coker won't let nobody wear No 4, so he put this No 4 up.

00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:20.218
"This No 4, like, it's retired till you get here."

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:23.304
To make a long story short, man, I sat out a whole year for nothing.

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:24.806
- What explanation they give you?

00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:25.556
-  It wasn't none.

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:27.642
They say, "You eligible now. You can come back and play."

00:04:27.642 --> 00:04:29.477
So I had to sit out a whole year for no reason.

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:30.812
That following year, man, 

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:31.896
they called me. 

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:34.107
They said, "Everything been cleared. 

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.149
You can come play now."

00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:37.068
- If you could talk to that coach right now 

00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:38.736
about the experience that you went through, 

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:39.904
what would you tell that coach?

00:04:39.904 --> 00:04:41.864
- Face to face, "Was it really you?"

00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:43.116
Was it you

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.159
or was it any of these other colleges that I've turned down? 

00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:49.247
It's nothing you can do now. My career is set in stone now. 
There's nothing you can take away from me.

00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:51.791
But holding me out a year, if it really was you, let me know. 

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.126
Like, I can swallow that pill.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.796
You're a coward for that. I don't respect you as a man."

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.131
- Go ahead and let you shoot, man.

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:02.135
- So coming off that year, you're still in Miami.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:02.552
- Yeah.

00:05:02.552 --> 00:05:04.178
You're back on track.

00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:05.096
- Mmhmm.

00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:06.139
- Back in college football.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:06.639
- Gotchu.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.683
- What's going on in your mindset as you're trying to get back in the flow?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:14.063
- I told my coach and I told all my close friends and my 
family members, I said, "Listen here, man.

00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:15.606
I don't care who we play. 

00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:19.068
But the first time I get the ball in the Orange Bowl, I'm taking it to the house."

00:05:19.068 --> 00:05:22.488
We on the sideline coming up the tunnel, and I told my strength coach, I said, "Listen here.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.366
If they kick it to me, I'm coming up out my helmet” 

00:05:25.366 --> 00:05:28.703
And I want that person who did that to look me in my face

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:29.954
when I'm crossing that end zone.

00:05:29.954 --> 00:05:31.331
I'm running through everybody. 

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:34.167
Full speed straight down the sideline. I cut it up. 

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.501
Sean Taylor led the block.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.627
- Rest in peace, Sean Taylor.

00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:38.171
- Led me through the hole, man, 

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.297
About the 5-yard line. 

00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:41.466
I'm switching the ball. I'm coming out my chin straps.

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:42.925
Touchdown against Florida Gators. 

00:05:42.925 --> 00:05:46.763
As soon as I cross the end zone, I'm flicking it off. 
I'm right in front of the camera like, "Yeah, 

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:47.764
I hope you see me."

00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:49.599
- [Laughing]

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:51.059
- I hope he sees you now too.

00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:53.061
- I hope he sees me, man. You know what I mean?

00:05:54.062 --> 00:05:55.897
- I really thought I was about to win this shit, man.

